# Prologue — hired at the gate, the town seen, the tower shut.
# Tone rules (CANON 6): warm, wry, gentle. Humour from character, never
# meanness. The Detective's choices are tone, never morals.

@node p_gate_open
  The road comes over the hill and Prismbrook is laid out below like a page
  somebody forgot to colour in.
  You have seen this town on a postcard. The postcard lied, or the town did.
  A man in a very good coat is waiting at the arch, holding his hat with both
  hands, which is not what hats are for.

@node p_mayor_gate
  [if flag p.hired == 0]
  MAYOR(worried): You came. Good. Yes. Good.
  MAYOR(worried): You will want the facts and I will give you the facts and
  then I would like very much to sit down.
  MAYOR: Yesterday this town was the brightest thing on this coast. This
  morning we woke up the colour of a wet newspaper.
  grant clue.town_gray
  MAYOR(sad): The Prism is gone out of the lantern room. Gone from its cradle.
  grant clue.prism_missing
  YOU:
    * (kind) That must have been a frightening thing to wake up to.  -> p_mayor_kind
    * (curious) Gone how? Taken, or simply not there?  -> p_mayor_curious
    * (dry) And the reward for finding it is the colour back, I take it.  -> p_mayor_dry
  [else]
  MAYOR: Whatever you need. Anything at all. Except — well. Whatever you need.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Anything except what, Mayor?  -> p_mayor_dodge
    * (kind) I will come back when I have something.  -> p_mayor_wave
  [end]

@node p_mayor_kind
  MAYOR(moved): It was. Thank you for saying so. Nobody has.
  goto p_mayor_terms

@node p_mayor_curious
  MAYOR: Not there. The door was shut. The door is still shut.
  goto p_mayor_terms

@node p_mayor_dry
  MAYOR(laughing): Ha. Yes. The reward is the colour back, and the council's
  savings, which I am afraid are mostly the colour back.
  goto p_mayor_terms

@node p_mayor_terms
  MAYOR: The council pooled what we had. It is not much and it is all of it.
  set p.hired = 1
  MAYOR: Go anywhere. Ask anyone. They will talk to you; they have been
  talking to each other about nothing else for a day.
  MAYOR(shifty): Only — start in the square. Not the tower. The tower can
  wait.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Why can the tower wait?  -> p_mayor_dodge
    * (kind) The square it is.  -> p_mayor_wave

@node p_mayor_dodge
  MAYOR(shifty): Because there is nothing at the tower but a locked door and
  an old man talking to it. Because — because it can wait.
  MAYOR: The square, detective. Please.

@node p_mayor_wave
  MAYOR(happy): Splendid. Splendid. I shall be here, holding my hat.

@node p_square_open
  The square is full of people not looking at each other, which in a town this
  size takes real effort.
  Something black and white comes off the fountain rim like a thrown stone,
  and every head in the square snaps up to follow it.
  It is a magpie. It goes over the roofs towards the tower, fast and low, and
  it does not look back.
  Somebody by the baker's says, quite clearly and to nobody, "There he goes.
  There goes the thief."

@node p_bruno
  [if flag p.met_bruno == 0]
  BRUNO(sad): You are the detective. Here. Take a bun.
  YOU:
    * (kind) That is very kind of you.  -> p_bruno_kind
    * (dry) Is this evidence?  -> p_bruno_dry
    * (curious) Why is everyone looking at the sky?  -> p_bruno_bird
  [else]
  BRUNO(happy): Still warm. Take another.
  goto p_bruno_bird
  [end]

@node p_bruno_kind
  BRUNO(moved): It is the only useful thing I know how to do before noon.
  trust bruno 1
  goto p_bruno_bird

@node p_bruno_dry
  BRUNO(laughing): Everything is evidence, that is what I always say. No I
  do not. Eat the bun.
  goto p_bruno_bird

@node p_bruno_bird
  set p.met_bruno = 1
  BRUNO(worried): The bird. Iris Marlow's magpie. Pip.
  BRUNO: Half this town has decided he flew off with the Prism in his beak,
  because he is shiny-minded and because it is easier than thinking.
  grant clue.magpie_blamed
  BRUNO(sad): I do not hold with it. He used to sit on my sill and I used to
  pretend to shoo him.
  YOU:
    * (kind) A magpie could not lift a crystal that size.  -> p_bruno_size
    * (curious) Who is Iris Marlow?  -> p_bruno_iris
    * (dry) People do like a suspect with feathers.  -> p_bruno_iris

@node p_bruno_size
  BRUNO(happy): No. He could not. I said so and I was told I was soft.
  trust bruno 1
  goto p_bruno_iris

@node p_bruno_iris
  BRUNO: Our Tinter. She keeps the Prism lit. Kept. Keeps.
  BRUNO(worried): She has a standing order with me. Two seeded rolls, every
  second day, forty years between her and her mother.
  BRUNO(sad): I baked them yesterday and they are still on the shelf.

@node p_wick_square
  [if flag p.met_wick == 0]
  WICK: Mm.
  WICK: You will be the one they wrote away for.
  YOU:
    * (kind) I am. And you are the one who keeps the tower.  -> p_wick_keeps
    * (curious) Has anyone actually been inside the Prismworks today?  -> p_wick_inside
    * (dry) Word travels.  -> p_wick_keeps
  [else]
  WICK: She is still shut. I have asked her twice today.
  goto p_wick_inside
  [end]

@node p_wick_keeps
  WICK(neutral): Forty-one years. She and I get on.
  set p.met_wick = 1
  goto p_wick_inside

@node p_wick_inside
  set p.met_wick = 1
  WICK(worried): Nobody has been in. Nobody can. She is locked.
  WICK: And here is the part that has the Mayor holding his hat. She is
  locked from the inside.
  grant clue.door_locked
  YOU:
    * (curious) Then whoever locked it never left.  -> p_wick_never
    * (kind) You sound worried about her. The tower, or the Tinter?  -> p_wick_both
    * (dry) A thief who tidies up after himself.  -> p_wick_never

@node p_wick_never
  WICK: Mm. That is the shape of it, aye.
  goto p_wick_iris

@node p_wick_both
  WICK(moved): ...Both. I am not much good at saying so.
  trust wick 1
  goto p_wick_iris

@node p_wick_iris
  WICK(sad): Iris Marlow has not been seen since last night. She goes quiet
  for a day sometimes. Not when the Prism goes quiet with her.
  grant clue.iris_missing
  WICK: Go up and look at her yourself. The Prismworks, I mean. The tower.
  WICK: You can stand on the stair. The stair is sound as far as it goes.

@node p_after_morning
  You look at what you have written and it does not add up to a theft. It
  adds up to a locked room with the wrong things missing.
  A theft takes something valuable. This took something valuable, and a
  person, and left the door locked behind it.
  set p.opened = 1
  MAYOR: Well? Well?
  YOU:
    * (kind) Somebody is inside that tower, Mayor. Or was.  -> p_after_kind
    * (dry) Your thief locked up behind himself and took the caretaker.  -> p_after_dry
    * (curious) Who saw the tower last night?  -> p_after_curious

@node p_after_kind
  MAYOR(worried): Inside. Oh dear. Oh dear.
  goto p_after_send

@node p_after_dry
  MAYOR(laughing): When you put it like that it does sound less like a
  magpie.
  goto p_after_send

@node p_after_curious
  MAYOR: The harbour, I should think. The harbour is awake at all hours.
  goto p_after_send

@node p_after_send
  MAYOR: The harbour. Otto Brine is down there and Otto Brine sees everything
  and says almost none of it.
  MAYOR(happy): Go on. Go and be a detective at them.
